From bd69a5105566c128412c3f37f9a9a1b1dfe609ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:23:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): durable placement cancellation across crash gap
 and send failures [daveey]

Archive and manual completion of a placed card now append placement_cancel_intent
in the same txn as the terminal flip. The dispatcher sweep replays an intent with
no forward event after it (crash between commit and forward), resends a failed
archive with capped exponential backoff, and gives up after 7 days with a comment.
A send that raised is recorded failed instead of lost; a completion whose remote
copy is already terminal records skipped. Settle completions record no intent and
are never cancelled. Resends reuse the deterministic hub request id.
